SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 47 spots lef
 t\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/
 events/203300\n\n1:00PM Program\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat does it take to 
 challenge convention\, build what doesn’t yet exist\, and turn ambitious
  ideas into meaningful change? In the latest edition of 90 Minutes of Inno
 vation\, John Werner - venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI c
 olumnist - sits down with Lauren Kuntz\, PhD\, Head of Market Analysis at
  ENGIE\, Gaiascope co-founder\, and founder of the Women’s Greatest Athl
 ete.\n\nWith degrees in Physics and Mechanical Engineering from MIT and a 
 PhD in Climate Science from Harvard\, Kuntz co-founded the Y Combinator-b
 acked energy forecasting startup Gaiascope\, using AI to advance renewable
  energy markets before its 2025 acquisition by ENGIE.\n\nKuntz has brought
  that same drive to the world of sport. A world-record holder in the 20-e
 vent double decathlon and three-time All-American\, she founded World’s
  Greatest Athlete in 2024 and the Women’s Decathlon World Championships�
 �to challenge one of track and field’s longstanding disparities: while
  men have competed in the Olympic decathalon since 1912\, women never have
 . Now\, she is helping build the case for the women’s decathlon to fina
 lly earn its place at the Olympic Games.\n\nTogether\, Werner and Kuntz wi
 ll explore what it means to pursue ideas before there is a roadmap\, chall
 enge deeply established systems\, and build something entirely new. From 
 rethinking the power grid to reimagining who gets to compete on the world�
 ��s biggest stage\, expect a wide-ranging conversation about seeing what c
 ould be—and having the nerve to build it. \n\n*This event is compliment
 ary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refresh
 ments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at leas
 t 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203300
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
